      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "5d63bc01c3595d2c8a2919f8532420d767e60f63",
            "subject": "LU-15909 lnet: use 64-bit selection sequence numbers"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-12 19:45:06.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-21 17:57:42.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-15909 lnet: spill sends to a net with a free credit",
        "message": "LU-15909 lnet: spill sends to a net with a free credit\n\nA peer can have a fast net and a slow net, for example o2ib and tcp.\nWith a UDSP priority rule on the fast net, every send uses that net.\nWhen the fast net has no free credit, LNet queues the message. The\nslow net stays idle, even when it has free credits.\n\nAdd the lnet_spillover tunable, default 0. When it is 1, LNet can\nselect again without the selected net. It does so only when every\nequal or better path on that net would queue the message. Health and\nselection priority decide which path is better. The new path must be\nas healthy. It must also have a free peer credit and a free NI credit.\n\nMove the latency_stats set and show code into shared helpers\nfor a boolean module parameter. The spillover tunable uses them.\n\n    lnetctl set spillover 1\n    lnetctl global show | grep spillover\n        spillover: 1\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I8724ddd72da48f86aec481de402ba404928787b4\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
